# Architecture boundaries

Offline-first Expo app. Local SQLite is the source of truth; Firebase is sync/auth/backup.

## Layers

- `features/` — screens only; compose UI; call repositories/domain
- `components/` — reusable UI; no repositories or Firebase
- `domain/` — pure TS business logic; no React, no SQLite
- `repositories/` — SQLite only; no screens
- `sync/` — queue/push/pull/conflicts; not feature UI
- `firebase/` — Auth + App Check wrappers only
- `application/` — AppRoot, navigators, event-bus

## Rules

- Never query SQLite from a screen — use a repository.
- Commit writes locally before any network call.
- Money is integer paise; IDs are UUID strings; soft-delete via `deleted_at`.
- Visible strings go through i18n keys (`en.json` / `hi.json`).
- Do not create `src/app/` (conflicts with Expo Router detection).
- Path alias: `@/*` → `src/*`.

